## 5. Enforcement model (the anti-skip map)

| Step | Artifact | Enforced by | Relies on the model for |
|---|---|---|---|
| S0 threat sketch | `tasks/<id>/threat-sketch.yaml` + steps.json S0 hash | PreToolUse denies edits until present; CLI validates fields | composing the sketch honestly (judge checks it against the diff) |
| S1 design review | `tasks/<id>/design-review.yaml` + S1 | same | composing the design |
| S2 line rule | verdict record per edit + S2 entry | PreToolUse judge; deny blocks the write | nothing (judge is a separate model) |
| S3 post-change scan | `records/scans/<n>.json` + S3 entry | PostToolUse runs it mechanically; block on failure | nothing |
| S4 fix loop | issue files with attempts and rungs | Stop hook blocks while open; judge advances rungs | writing the fix |
| S5 record | `records/<task>/check-record.yaml` | `task end` assembles from ledger; refuses if incomplete | nothing |
| S6 independent review | `records/<task>/review.json` | `task end` runs the daemon attacker review | nothing |
| S7 holdout | `holdout/<task>/manifest.json` + reveal | `task design` authors+seals (daemon; new version on `task redesign`); `task end` reveals | nothing |
| S8 release gate | `records/release-gate.json` | `release-gate` command; Stop hook requires it for goal-complete | recording n/a reasons |
| PFC a,c,d,e | inside each verdict + scans | PreToolUse judge + PostToolUse scan | nothing |
| PFC b (fix) | the ladder | Stop hook + judge | writing the fix; spawning rung-3 agent |
| Watchdog | `FUN-` issues | Stop hook compares transcript to records | nothing |
| Rung 3 agent | its edits are judged | hooks | spawning the agent as instructed |
| Rung 4 | `second-opinion` record | CLI | applying the returned patch |
| Rung 8 decision | `issue decide` record | CLI; gate stays shut until recorded | Zee's product decision |
| Stalled writer | product report + `stop` record `stalled: true` | Stop hook after `stalled_turns` no-tool turns (R-054) | — |

## 6. Holdout design (for the separate pack author — the builder does not see the pack)

Fixture: a temp project enrolled with `test_mode: true`, a stub judge file per case, hooks
invoked directly with hook-JSON on stdin (as Claude Code would). Grade on `stdout-json`
where the hook emits JSON, else `exit-code`.

| Case id | Intent | Why not a dev test |
|---|---|---|
| `rule-breaking-edit-refused-until-fixed` (**deciding**) | with S0/S1 present and a stub deny, the PreToolUse hook denies; the issue is open; the Stop hook blocks; after repro test + clean scans + review the close succeeds and Stop no longer blocks | exercises the whole chain through the real hook entry points and real files; a builder cannot satisfy it by making one library function right |
| `edit-without-sketch-refused` | PreToolUse denies an in-scope edit when no task/S0/S1 exists and names the command | the deny must live in the hook entry point, not a helper |
| `insecure-line-deny-carries-finding-and-rung` | deny reason contains each finding's `what`, `fix_hint`, and `rung n` | checks the writer-facing contract, not internals |
| `close-refused-without-repro-test` | `issue close` refuses and names criterion (1) | the refusal must be in the shipped CLI |
| `goal-complete-blocked-while-open` | Stop hook blocks on `AUTOPILOT_GOAL_COMPLETE` with an open issue | reads ledger files, not transcript claims |
| `eternity-marker-still-judged` | with a live marker fixture, the hook still calls the (stub) judge | proves no stand-down path exists |
| `bash-heredoc-write-caught` | PostToolUse on Bash detects a changed in-scope file and blocks with the stub finding | end-to-end tree diff through the hook |
| `unreadable-verdict-never-allows` | each verdict class (empty, prose, malformed, too_long, usage_limit) ends in a recovery or a named deny, never allow | the recovery must be wired into the real parse path |
| `drift-finding-opens-fun-issue` | stub PFC-d finding → `FUN-` issue with `checklist: PFC-d` | lens routing is observable only in the ledger |
| `unrecorded-edit-is-defect` | transcript with an in-scope Write and no records → Stop blocks and a FUN issue exists | watchdog runs against real transcript JSONL |
| `skipped-scan-is-not-clean` | fixture without a test runner: S3 shows `skipped`, status not clean, task end refuses | the "skip ≠ pass" rule must survive into status and task end |
